For each word below, write ONE short sentence (12 to 22 words) that uses the word itself, spelled in full, in the sense given. Give it voice and mood: a question, someone speaking, a sigh, delight, a warning. No definitions; show the word in a moment of life. Answer as one JSON object mapping each WORD (as given, upper case) to its sentence. JSON only.

TUMBLER: a gymnast who performs rolls and somersaults and twists.
WATCH: a small portable timepiece.
WAVE: one of a series of ridges that moves across the surface of a liquid (especially across a large body of water).
WAVELENGTH: the distance (measured in the direction of propagation) between two points in the same phase in consecutive cycles of a wave.
WEBSITE: a computer connected to the internet that maintains a series of web pages on the World Wide Web.
WEIGHT: the vertical force exerted by a mass as a result of gravity.
